[issue.1842]
number = 1842
title = "[Coherence] Decision 2881 and do_15 say the wallet send and token transfer examples already carry --gateway-rpc, but they do not, and send also needs it"
revision = "3520b1428059af90261432778c008a9ce362a0b1"
verdict = "spec-edit"
evidence = "Correct decision 2881's basis at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:10402 and completed task 22.39.118 (status at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:188428), do_15 at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:188466, to say that all ten examples lacked --gateway-rpc in commit 61b1cd9c81e4070dc5dfccd4bb9255c602cfb066, including send and transfer, and that commit a08a60044bf3f1a66189338037862089c11b31f0 supplied the hosted URL for all ten using the supported options: the six writes and both balance examples now carry --gateway-rpc (tools/platform/cli/README.md:222, :227, :231, :236, :241, :246, :331, :334), matching the mandatory hosted account client at tools/platform/cli/src/wallet.rs:1026 called by Send at :1064 and exercised by tools/platform/cli/tests/repair_22_33_1499.rs:666, while token info/list use the hosted URL through --rpc (tools/platform/cli/README.md:325, :335, :336) because their declarations have no gateway option (tools/platform/cli/src/wallet.rs:204) and read_asset passes rpc to sdk_rpc at :908."
close_comment = "The README now supplies the hosted service URL for wallet send and token transfer, and its integration test exercises both examples. The remaining correction is to the completed task and decision text: send and transfer also lacked the option in the original revision, while token info and list select their hosted endpoint with --rpc."
